00:24:42.480 --> 00:24:43.660
that I did before.

00:24:43.660 --> 00:24:46.590
Kube CTL, apply.

00:24:46.590 --> 00:24:48.900
Now if I do get pods--

00:24:48.900 --> 00:24:51.650
Oops, I got to do it quick.

00:24:51.650 --> 00:24:53.370
They're already up.

00:24:53.370 --> 00:24:56.600
That wasn't that wasn't good,
because you didn't actually see

00:24:56.600 --> 00:24:59.021
that they weren't out before.

00:24:59.021 --> 00:24:59.520
Yeah?

00:25:03.460 --> 00:25:06.905
AUDIENCE: What means
[INAUDIBLE] ready, two over two?

00:25:06.905 --> 00:25:08.280
BRENT SHAFFER:
OK, good question.

00:25:08.280 --> 00:25:11.600
So this is a list of the pods.

00:25:11.600 --> 00:25:14.390
And inside ready
is the containers.

00:25:14.390 --> 00:25:16.530
So two of two
containers are ready.

00:25:16.530 --> 00:25:20.090
So for our Faceswap
worker pod, we

00:25:20.090 --> 00:25:21.440
have just one container running.

00:25:21.440 --> 00:25:24.800
And that's the face swap script.

00:25:24.800 --> 00:25:28.640
For our WordPress worker,
or our WordPress pods,

00:25:28.640 --> 00:25:31.040
we have two containers inside.

00:25:31.040 --> 00:25:35.720
One is for the actual face
swap WordPress container.

00:25:35.720 --> 00:25:37.860
That we built and deployed
that we talked about.

00:25:37.860 --> 00:25:40.490
And one is something that I
didn't talk about, because I

00:25:40.490 --> 00:25:43.070
didn't want to confuse anybody.

00:25:43.070 --> 00:25:44.270
But it's not that confusing.

00:25:44.270 --> 00:25:51.110
So there is a Cloud SQL proxy
running in another container.

00:25:51.110 --> 00:25:52.220
This Cloud SQL proxy.

00:25:57.300 --> 00:25:58.910
So if we look at
this original file

00:25:58.910 --> 00:26:03.170
that I had after this
container configuration,

00:26:03.170 --> 00:26:05.960
I have another
container configuration

00:26:05.960 --> 00:26:11.540
that basically spins up
from another container

00:26:11.540 --> 00:26:13.130
image a proxy server.

00:26:13.130 --> 00:26:17.390
So the WordPress
instance is communicating

00:26:17.390 --> 00:26:20.150
with a proxy server, which
communicates a Cloud SQL.

00:26:20.150 --> 00:26:22.219
And that's how Cloud
SQL version two works.

00:26:22.219 --> 00:26:24.260
I don't know if anybody
here that works at Google

00:26:24.260 --> 00:26:25.970
has a good explanation
for why that is.

00:26:25.970 --> 00:26:27.270
I don't actually know.

00:26:27.270 --> 00:26:31.820
But if you use something like
spanner, which is something

00:26:31.820 --> 00:26:33.080
we announced recently.

00:26:33.080 --> 00:26:37.030
And it's an awesome database.

00:26:37.030 --> 00:26:38.450
You won't need to do that.

00:26:38.450 --> 00:26:41.630
You'll just connect
directly to it.

00:26:41.630 --> 00:26:46.286
But that's good,
because it illustrates

